    {
      "name": "richTextBox2",
      "kind": "RichTextBox",
      "parent": "wp_ElevationModel",
      "index": 2,
      "text": "Elevation models are essential for work with AirScout. They are needed for calculating radio horizons and propagation paths.\nThe software can handle the most common models available for the public:\n\nGLOBE: 1km x 1km resolution, covers whole earth\nSRTM3: 90m x 90m resolution, covers only -60° ... +60° (with some inoffical extensions to Norh)\nSRTM1: 30m x 30m resolution, covers only -60° ... +60°\nASTER3: 90m x 90m resolution, covers -83° ... +83° (aggregated from ASTER1, very raw data )\nASTER1: 30m x 30m resolution, covers -83° ... +83° (very raw data)\n\nElevation data are provided in files. AirScout is trying to download and stores them locally. If you have them already somewhere on your computer, you can select a user specific path.\n\nYou must choose at least one elevation model to continue.",
      "location": [
        13,
        13
      ],
      "size": [
        558,
        212
      ],
      "dock": null,
